{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103062","id":2346643851,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6L3vGL","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103062","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103062.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103062.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103062","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103062/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103062/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103062/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3c9066a62e2473a65ed541288bd056b7dd9b7975","number":103062,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add support for offscreen rendering","user":{"login":"PiCode9560","id":122909224,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1NyKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122909224?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560","html_url":"https://github.com/PiCode9560","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implement https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/5790\r\n- Add `MODE_OFFSCREEN` `Mode` to `Window`.\r\n- Adds `--offscreen` CLI flag, which use `MODE_OFFSCREEN` on the main window.\r\n- `--resolution` change the resolution of the viewport if using `--offscreen` and the `stretch_mode` set to \"viewport\".\r\n- Only work on Windows. It will probably just break or just not work if tried on other OS.\r\n- Currently, it was made for OpenGL renderer. **Not tested**, but it should also work for Vulkan.\r\n- It still creates a window, because OpenGL FrameBuffer Object cannot be used without it. However, the window is minimized and removed from the taskbar. For Vulkan, the window can be removed in the future.\r\n- The offscreen viewport size is still depended on the window size, unless using the \"viewport\" stretch mode, of course.\r\n\r\n## Sample Project\r\n\r\nSample project: [offscreentest.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18885733/offscreentest.zip)\r\n\r\n\r\n(The project may need to be opened normally in-editor first for assets to be imported.)\r\n\r\nThis project has a scene with a rotating cube and some music. It saves screenshots at a set interval to the snaps folder (only up to 10 images should be saved, in png format).\r\n\r\nSuggested methods of testing:\r\n\r\n- `godot.exe --offscreen`\r\n  - This uses the offscreen window mode and no other changes. Audio should still work. Snapshots should appear in the snaps folder.\r\n- `godot.exe --offscreen --write-movie output.avi`\r\n  - Uses the offscreen window mode, but also runs in movie mode. The resulting movie file should show the spinning cube.\r\n\r\n## Implementation Notes\r\n- It was implemented as `WindowMode`, so that all windows can independently be offscreen. Not sure if it's better to add it as a separate window option like `window.offscreen = false/true`, or just make it an option only for the main window.\r\n- Hiding window from taskbar implementation is stolen from #99856\r\n\r\n## To do\r\n- Remove window when using offscreen on Vulkan.\r\n- **Maybe** add support for other platform like Linux and macOS. (I don't have any of these OS, so it would be hard to test)","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5790,"closed_issues":0,"cr